WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.875
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 2, Network implementation, which is 20 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.875 --> 00:00:10.478
This lesson covers objective 2 point 3.

00:00:10.478 --> 00:00:15.352
Given a scenario, select and configure wireless devices and technologies.

00:00:15.352 --> 00:00:21.360
Today's concept: what changes, and what does not, when a user roams between access points.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.430
Two access points broadcast the same network name, Office.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.360
That shared name is the ESSID.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.960
But each access point radio has its own hardware address, the BSSID.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.869
A user sits near the first access point.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:39.760
The laptop is associated with BSSID zero one.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.134
The user walks across the building.

00:00:42.134 --> 00:00:44.690
The laptop moves to the second access point.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.715
The BSSID changed from zero one to zero two.

00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:50.950
The ESSID stayed Office, so the user notices nothing.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.762
For the exam, the network name is the ESSID, and it stays the same while you roam.

00:00:59.762 --> 00:01:03.892
The BSSID identifies each access point's radio, so it changes.

00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:06.090
That's objective two point three.
